{"title":"Career roadmap · Theatre Artist","role":"Theatre Artist","summary":"A Theatre Artist creates and performs theatre through acting, movement, voice, direction, writing, production and collaborative performance. A BA in Dance/Theatre/Performing Arts provides the foundation for performance technique, theatre history, movement, voice, dramatic interpretation and stagecraft.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career alignment"},{"type":"p","text":"A Theatre Artist creates and performs theatre through acting, movement, voice, direction, writing, production and collaborative performance. A BA in Dance/Theatre/Performing Arts provides the foundation for performance technique, theatre history, movement, voice, dramatic interpretation and stagecraft."},{"type":"p","text":"Because theatre is portfolio- and performance-driven, employability depends heavily on practical stage experience, audition readiness, performance credits, networking and a strong showreel/portfolio, rather than academic qualifications alone."},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BA Performing Arts","Acting/Performance Training","Theatre Productions","Portfolio + Showreel","Theatre Artist","Specialist/Lead Performer","Theatre Director/Creative Professional"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Roles","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Student"},{"text":"Theatre Performer, Theatre Intern"},{"text":"Training and stage experience"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Theatre Artist, Actor, Ensemble Performer"},{"text":"Live performance"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"Professional Theatre Artist, Supporting Actor"},{"text":"Regular productions"}],[{"text":"Specialist"},{"text":"Character Actor, Movement Artist, Voice Artist"},{"text":"Performance specialisation"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"Lead Theatre Artist,